{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"singleton pattern singleton pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","fileName":"Singleton Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Singleton Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"singleton pattern singleton pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","fileName":"Singleton Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Singleton Pattern","heading":"Singleton Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The singleton pattern constrains a class to one instance within a chosen application boundary. The book uses a single inventory context so commands observe the same in-memory book collection, then shows how a .NET service container can manage that lifetime. One instance is not the same as thread safety: concurrent mutation still requires coordination. A singleton can also hide global state and create a bottleneck, so it should be used only when shared identity is a real requirement.\n\nSingleton centralizes access to one class instance across an application, but instance count alone does not make the object's state safe or its lifetime appropriate. The source's connection-configuration example illustrates the wish for one source of settings, which is distinct from requiring only one physical database connection.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"singleton pattern singleton pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Singleton Pattern.md","fileName":"Singleton Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Singleton Pattern","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}